      "head_commit": {
        "id": "42dc8a3b84fbbbfe2c1d19a1d67c63c9bc086908",
        "tree_id": "42256604c70a368c6eca26ec79e59a93e39cc74f",
        "message": "feat(NET-005): server-authoritative anim state machine and clip manifest\n\nThe machine lives in core so client and server run the same transitions (D86)\nwhile the server keeps authority (I1). IDLE -> TRANSITIONING -> LOCOMOTION ->\nACTION -> RECOVERY -> IDLE: a 2-tick blend, a 3-tick recovery, and an action\nthat ends at transitionTick + duration. A request during ACTION is refused\n(busy); during RECOVERY it is queued to the last recovery tick. Two queued\nrequests collapse to the smallest (sequence, clipId), the tie-break GDD §8.4\nnames.\n\nThe clip manifest is validated on load: locomotion loops, action does not,\nevents stay inside the clip and are strictly ordered, ids are unique. The\npublished JSON Schema is asserted by a test to share the code's enums and\nrequired fields, so the two cannot drift silently.\n\nGDD-ANIM-ARCHITECTURE 0.2 -> 0.3 (I9): state table, 12-byte anim_state,\nsourced windows, queue/tie-break edge cases. The corrupted open-questions\ntable is repaired; the missing 0.2 changelog row is left missing rather than\ninvented.\n\nAcceptance: anim 22/22, full 73/73, verify 17/17, typecheck 0, core-math 0,\nGDD 0, blueprint 0, tracer green. The blueprint acc was repaired twice: the\nfirst repair to -t animstate exited 0 while skipping all 41 tests (false\npass), so the acc now names the test file. Both failing forms are logged.\n\nAgent: animation-director\nTask: NET-005",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-18T08:44:56Z",
